{"_id":"68a7363c8ec3d8323af1f14a","nodeId":"aaua13CkTxLOYXr8cAgPm","roadmapSlug":"sql","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:40.099Z","description":"# INNER JOIN\n\nINNER JOINs combine rows from two or more tables based on a related column. They return only the rows where there is a match in the specified columns of all tables involved in the join. If there's no matching value in the joined columns, that row is excluded from the result set.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"SQL INNER JOIN Clause","url":"https://www.programiz.com/sql/inner-join","_id":"69bba6b933a0ad7a57afe6ea"}],"updatedAt":"2026-03-19T07:33:13.507Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e04dcfb5fcb94d0416838","title":"DataCamp - SQL Fundamentals","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/ZVeXng"},{"_id":"6a5e04dcfb5fcb94d04167c7","title":"roadmap.sh - Master SQL","partner":"roadmap.sh","type":"course","url":"https://roadmap.sh/courses/sql"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/sql/content/aaua13CkTxLOYXr8cAgPm.md"}